<!-- How ROSRA Works — methodology walkthrough with sample-report screenshots -->
<section id="rosra-methodology" class="uh-section">
    <div class="container">
        <h2 class="uh-section-title">How ROSRA Works</h2>
        <p class="uh-section-subtitle">A four-step methodology that turns own-source revenue data into a concrete reform plan. Each screenshot below is from the Nairobi sample report.</p>

        <!-- Step 1 — Gap Analysis (image left, text right) -->
        <div class="rosra-method-row">
            <div class="rosra-method-img">
                <img src="~/images/methodology/step1-gap-analysis.png"
                     alt="Step 1 Gap Analysis dashboard showing the property tax matrix and revenue vs potential breakdown"
                     loading="lazy" />
            </div>
            <div class="rosra-method-text">
                <span class="rosra-method-step">Step 1</span>
                <h3 class="rosra-method-heading"><i class="fas fa-magnifying-glass-chart me-2"></i>Gap Analysis</h3>
                <p>For each revenue stream, the city enters only the inputs in the gray-shaded cells — registered units, billed amount, outstanding amount, statutory benchmark — and ROSRA decomposes the gap between current collection and full potential into specific drivers: <strong>Compliance</strong>, <strong>Coverage</strong>, <strong>Valuation</strong> or <strong>Liability</strong>, and the mixed gaps that combine them. The matrix dashboard on the right makes it instantly visible where each shilling is slipping through. Streams that don't apply to your context (e.g. Solid Waste Fee here) can be excluded.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Step 2 — Prioritization (image right, text left) -->
        <div class="rosra-method-row rosra-method-row--reverse">
            <div class="rosra-method-img">
                <img src="~/images/methodology/step2-prioritization.png"
                     alt="Step 2 Stream Prioritization table showing each revenue stream ranked by total functional gap"
                     loading="lazy" />
            </div>
            <div class="rosra-method-text">
                <span class="rosra-method-step">Step 2</span>
                <h3 class="rosra-method-heading"><i class="fas fa-sort-amount-down me-2"></i>Prioritization</h3>
                <p>Streams are ranked by their Total Functional Gap and broken down per gap-type — Compliance, Coverage, Valuation/Liability, and the mixed gaps — in a single stacked bar so the city can see at a glance which reforms move the most revenue. Decision-makers can <strong>re-order, exclude, or remove specific gap-types</strong> that aren't politically feasible. Excluded streams (like Solid Waste Fee here) are dropped from rank, share, the bar chart, and the downstream Recommendations — the plan respects local realities, not just the math.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Step 3 — Overview Selection (image left, text right) -->
        <div class="rosra-method-row">
            <div class="rosra-method-img">
                <img src="~/images/methodology/step3-overview-selection.png"
                     alt="Step 3 Overview Selection — solution cards with implementation guidance"
                     loading="lazy" />
            </div>
            <div class="rosra-method-text">
                <span class="rosra-method-step">Step 3</span>
                <h3 class="rosra-method-heading"><i class="fas fa-list-check me-2"></i>Overview Selection</h3>
                <p>From a curated library of <strong>82 evidence-based solution cards</strong>, ROSRA narrows the list by stream, gap-type, timeline, and political feasibility — and a 3-question personaliser tailors them to the city's context. Each card explains <em>what the option does</em>, <em>most useful when</em>, <em>usually not the best first move when</em>, and <em>often works best alongside</em>. The right-hand <strong>Selection Summary</strong> tracks every pick by stream and gap, with a one-click jump straight to Recommendations once you have enough.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Step 4 — Recommendations (image right, text left) -->
        <div class="rosra-method-row rosra-method-row--reverse">
            <div class="rosra-method-img">
                <img src="~/images/methodology/step4-recommendations.png"
                     alt="Step 4 Recommendations — consolidated action plan with timelines and quick-win tags"
                     loading="lazy" />
            </div>
            <div class="rosra-method-text">
                <span class="rosra-method-step">Step 4</span>
                <h3 class="rosra-method-heading"><i class="fas fa-lightbulb me-2"></i>Recommendations</h3>
                <p>The selected solutions are consolidated into a single implementation plan, grouped by stream and ranked by priority, with each card timeline-tagged as a <strong>Quick Win</strong> (&lt;1 year), <strong>Medium Term</strong> (1–3 years), or <strong>Long Term</strong> (3+ years). Switch between Solution Cards, Timeline View, and Progress Tracker views — then export the whole plan to PDF or HTML as the city's tailored Revenue Enhancement Action Plan.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="text-center mt-5">
            <a href="@Url.Action("SampleReports", "Home")" class="uh-btn uh-btn--outline">
                <i class="fas fa-eye me-2"></i>Explore the Sample Report
            </a>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

@section Scripts {
    <script>
        // Smooth scrolling for anchor links
        document.querySelectorAll('a[href^="#"]').forEach(anchor => {
            anchor.addEventListener('click', function (e) {
                e.preventDefault();
                const target = document.querySelector(this.getAttribute('href'));
                if (target) {
                    target.scrollIntoView({
                        behavior: 'smooth',
                        block: 'start'
                    });
                }
            });
        });

        // Animation on scroll
        const observerOptions = {
            root: null,
            rootMargin: '0px',
            threshold: 0.1
        };

        const observer = new IntersectionObserver((entries) => {
            entries.forEach(entry => {
                if (entry.isIntersecting) {
                    entry.target.classList.add('animate-in');
                }
            });
        }, observerOptions);

        document.querySelectorAll('.uh-info-card, .uh-pub-card, .uh-focus-item, .uh-flagship-card').forEach(el => {
            observer.observe(el);
        });

        // Hero slider
        (function() {
            const slides = document.querySelectorAll('.hero-slide');
            const indicators = document.querySelectorAll('.hero-indicators .indicator');
            let current = 0;
            let timer;

            function goTo(index) {
                slides[current].classList.remove('active');
                indicators[current].classList.remove('active');
                current = index;
                slides[current].classList.add('active');
                indicators[current].classList.add('active');
            }

            function next() {
                goTo((current + 1) % slides.length);
            }

            function startTimer() {
                timer = setInterval(next, 5000);
            }

            indicators.forEach(dot => {
                dot.addEventListener('click', function() {
                    clearInterval(timer);
                    goTo(parseInt(this.dataset.slide));
                    startTimer();
                });
            });

            startTimer();
        })();

        // Carousel controls for .uh-scroll-row (mobile/tablet only)
        document.querySelectorAll('.uh-carousel').forEach(carousel => {
            const row = carousel.querySelector('.uh-scroll-row');
            const prev = carousel.querySelector('.uh-carousel__btn--prev');
            const next = carousel.querySelector('.uh-carousel__btn--next');
            const dotsContainer = carousel.querySelector('.uh-carousel__dots');
            if (!row || !prev || !next || !dotsContainer) return;

            const cards = Array.from(row.querySelectorAll('.uh-pub-card'));
            if (!cards.length) return;

            cards.forEach((card, i) => {
                const dot = document.createElement('button');
                dot.type = 'button';
                dot.className = 'uh-carousel__dot';
                dot.setAttribute('aria-label', 'Go to slide ' + (i + 1));
                dot.addEventListener('click', () => {
                    row.scrollTo({ left: card.offsetLeft - row.offsetLeft, behavior: 'smooth' });
                });
                dotsContainer.appendChild(dot);
            });
            const dots = Array.from(dotsContainer.querySelectorAll('.uh-carousel__dot'));

            function update() {
                const rowLeft = row.getBoundingClientRect().left;
                let closestIndex = 0, minDist = Infinity;
                cards.forEach((c, i) => {
                    const dist = Math.abs(c.getBoundingClientRect().left - rowLeft);
                    if (dist < minDist) { minDist = dist; closestIndex = i; }
                });
                dots.forEach((d, i) => d.classList.toggle('is-active', i === closestIndex));
                prev.disabled = row.scrollLeft <= 2;
                next.disabled = row.scrollLeft + row.clientWidth >= row.scrollWidth - 2;
            }

            function step(direction) {
                const first = cards[0];
                const stepSize = first.getBoundingClientRect().width + 12;
                row.scrollBy({ left: direction * stepSize, behavior: 'smooth' });
            }

            prev.addEventListener('click', () => step(-1));
            next.addEventListener('click', () => step(1));
            row.addEventListener('scroll', update, { passive: true });
            window.addEventListener('resize', update);
            update();
        });
    </script>
}
